ough French doors into a serene backyard oasis, perfect for entertaining, weekend barbecues, or quiet evenings on the ""Queen's Necklace Viewing Deck."" The expansive rose garden, complete with a storybook gazebo, offers an idyllic setting for morning coffee or sunset relaxation. This versatile outdoor space also presents exciting possibilities for a future pickleball court, a resort-style pool, or putting green.Inside, the home offers two spacious living rooms with ocean and garden vistas, a formal dining room, and a tranquil primary suite with dual vanities, a soaking tub, and a separate shower. Two additional guest suites include private en-suite baths, while the optional fourth bedroom/office provides flexible space for work or guests. Additional highlights include hardwood flooring throughout, central air conditioning, a large circular driveway, and an attached two-car garage.Meticulously refreshed and restored by the current owner, this residence is truly move-in ready. Located within the award-winning Palos Verdes School District and just minutes from the beach, this estate invites you to fully embrace the sought-after Palos Verdes lifestyle.","","Entry, Family Room, Living Room","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","","","","","","","","","False","Full Service","Showing Instructions: Text or Call Listing Agent office line: (424)-241-3311. Please give at least 24 hours notice for showings. Showing Information: 24-hr Notice,Call LA 1 ","True","None","False","","3119","Assessor","","CA","Expired","One","","","Granvia Altamira","","1300","","","Ranch","Cash, Conventional","","","","Single Family Residence","","","City Lights, Coastline, Mountain(s), Ocean","True","","","Double Pane Windows, Skylight(s)","1955","90274","2006","PVR1*"
